# Test Automation Framework

This is a modular and scalable test automation framework built using **Java**, **Selenium WebDriver**, **Cucumber BDD**, **JUnit**, **Page Object Model (POM)**, and **Maven**. It is designed to support testing multiple applications with clean separation, reusability, and maintainability.

## 📦 Tech Stack

- **Language**: Java
- **Build Tool**: Maven
- **Test Runner**: JUnit
- **Automation**: Selenium WebDriver
- **BDD Framework**: Cucumber
- **Design Pattern**: Page Object Model (POM)
- **Version Control**: Git (with GitLab integration)
- **CI/CD**: GitLab CI (YAML-based pipeline)

🚀 Installation
Before installing the project, make sure you meet the following prerequisites:
✅ Access to the GitLab Repository
You must have access to the private GitLab repository. If you don't have access yet, please contact the administrator to request permission.

Once the prerequisites are met, follow these steps:
# Clone the repository
git clone https://gitlab.com/your-repo-url

# Navigate into the project directory
cd project-root

# Build the project and download dependencies
mvn clean install


🧪 Running Tests
Run all tests:
mvn test
Run a specific tag:
mvn test -Dcucumber.filter.tags="@SmokeTest"

🛠 Configuration
All configurations such as environment URLs, browser settings, and credentials are managed in the config.properties or environment-specific property files.
📄 Reporting
Cucumber HTML Reports are generated under the /target/cucumber-reports directory after each test run.

🔄 CI/CD Integration
This project is integrated with GitLab CI using a .gitlab-ci.yml file that supports:
Build and test stages
Report publishing
Environment targeting

👥 Contributing
We welcome contributions. Please follow our branching strategy and commit conventions.
